# Review instructions (REVIEW.md — copy to repo root)

> Read by the PR review loop (`/review`, `/mr-review`, managed Code Review or `claude-code-action`).
> Tech lead owns this file. Tune monthly: rate findings, cap nits, exclude generated paths.

## Passes
Run three passes and tag each finding with its pass:
- Bugs: logic errors, broken edge cases, subtle regressions
- Security: injection risks, authentication gaps, PII in logs
- Compliance: the change matches `intent.md`, `SPEC-<KEY>.md`, `tasks/<KEY>-plan.md` and design principles

## What Important means here
Reserve Important for findings that would break behavior, leak data, or breach a policy.
Style and naming are nits. One Critical = Request changes alone.

## Cap the nits
Report at most five nits per review; summarize the rest as a count.

## Do not report
- Generated files under `src/gen/` (adjust to repo)
- Anything CI already enforces (lint, format, typecheck)

## Threshold
Findings never approve or block alone. Branch protection requires code-owner approval.
A machine-readable severity tally may gate merges (platform-owned).
